OL,3,GNEWSAHomeless families given
OL,4,Aalternative to hotel living
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I had tears in my eyes because it's a
OL,7,Fnew start for my children. It might not
OL,8,Fbe where we need to be at but it's my
OL,9,Ffinal stepping stone to my forever
OL,10,Fhome."
OL,12,FMarie, not her real name, is among the
OL,13,Frecord 2,000 Bristol families living in
OL,14,Ftemporary accommodation, costing the
OL,15,Fcity council about #20m a year.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1789019766
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSAHomeless families given
OL,4,Aalternative to hotel living
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut after three years of being moved
OL,7,Fbetween hotels and sharing a bed with
OL,8,Fher 11-year-old son, she is about to
OL,9,Fmove into a new housing scheme aiming
OL,10,Fto cut the council's costs while giving
OL,11,Fhomeless families a better place to
OL,12,Flive.
OL,14,FThese five two-bed modular homes in
OL,15,Fsouth Bristol were built in a factory
OL,16,Fby housing association Places For
OL,17,FPeople (PFP), who say this is part of
OL,18,Fthe solution to the temporary
OL,19,Faccommodation crisis.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
